(N'166', N'youtube', N'2024 and beyond - In my honest opinion, this is one of the most unobtrusive, spirited, and purest singing artistry in “I Am A Singer”. Her sonorous voice simply just cuts through you like a sharp knife. It is also a solid testament that music trespasses boundaries of race, skin color, or background. Needless to say, she is from the Ulaanbaatar tribe, and her voice reverberates deeply within the roots. Set aside all those complex skills and showoffs, I finally understand the most critical aspect of singing is to stir powerful emotions within the listeners. Indeed, a polished, otherworldly gem in Mongolia&#39;s inhibit - Sitar Tan Wei Wei. This song will be stuck in my mind for a while. ❤️❤️❤️', N'6', NULL),
