(N'159', N'youtube', N'Music is impressive but the story behind it is even captivating and amazing. According to the legend Bo Ya(伯牙) author of this music was a talented musician. He put all his emotion into his music but no one could understand its meaning. Once he played and then noticed woodcutter(Zhong Zi Qi) who truly listened to his music. This man was able to portray the feelings and meaning of music just by listening to. For example, when Bo Ya played a tune praising the high mountains, Zhong Zi Qi said: “This tune is as magnificent and majestic as Mount Tai reaching to heaven!” When he played a work describing restless waves, the lumberjack said: “And this melody is as long and powerful as the great rivers!” All that Bo I wanted to express in my game, then Zi Tzu instantly and very accurately understood. They agreed that Bo Ya would visit Zhong Zi Qi again when he returned from his trip. Bo I kept my word and returned to Zi Zi. But it turned out that he had already died from the disease. Near the tomb of Tzu Tzu, devastated by grief, Bo Ya knelt before his Qin and began playing his melody “High Mountains, Flowing Water” (高山流水) for the last time. When the last note sounded, sobbing Bo Ya said: “From now on, there is no longer anyone who understands my music!” - and broke his qin on the gravestone. He never played again. And now the person who understands the feeling that the artist wants to portray called Zhiyin(知音) named Bosom Friend. It also means soulmate and. Tragedy is that Bo Ya lost his Zhiyin', N'69', NULL),
